=== STDOUT ===
~<N>ms  === a timer and a top-level await ===
~<N>ms  await: slept 20ms
~<N>ms  timer: 40ms, fired while the module was parked
~<N>ms  await: slept another 40ms
~<N>ms  === a read and a timer, issued together ===
~<N>ms  read: back first, first line is "// The event loop: one loop, waiting on timers and I/O at the same time."
~<N>ms  timer: 30ms deadline, reached second
~<N>ms  === setInterval ===
~<N>ms  interval: tick 1
~<N>ms  interval: tick 2
~<N>ms  interval: tick 3
~<N>ms  done: nothing left to wait for, so the loop exits

